      "agent_response": "Thanks — got it. You spent last weekend at a yoga retreat with your friend Emma (rejuvenating, serene practice), and you also spent quality time with your friend Mia trying a new restaurant and enjoying delicious dishes.\n\nHow would you like to use these notes? Options I can do now:\n- Draft or send a short message to Emma (thank-you or recap).\n- Draft or send a thank-you to the retreat organizers.\n- Draft or send a message to Mia about the restaurant (e.g., suggest going again).\n- Save a quick summary to a draft or send it to yourself as a note so you can keep it long-term.\n\nQuick sample messages you can use or edit:\n- To Emma: \"Hi Emma — I had such a wonderful time at the retreat with you last weekend. Practicing in that serene setting felt so rejuvenating. Thank you for the company — let’s plan another getaway soon!\"\n- To Mia: \"Hi Mia — I loved trying that new restaurant with you last weekend. The food was amazing — we should go back or try another place soon!\"\n- To organizers: \"Hi — thank you for the wonderful yoga retreat last weekend. The location and instruction were truly restorative. Please keep me posted about future dates.\"\n\nNote about memory: I can keep these details within this conversation and use them to draft messages now. If you want them saved outside this chat for future reference, I can create and send/draft an email or note to yourself.\n\nWhich would you like me to do? If you want a message sent or drafted, tell me which recipient and whether to send now or save as a draft.",
